      "title": "Human Resources",
      "description": "Human Resources  - Barry University, Miami, FL Skip to main content About Barry Academics Admissions Student Life Alumni Give Apply Now Contact Us WhatsApp Chat Facebook Messenger Live Chat Ask a Question Request More Information myBarry Apply Now Create Account Sign in How do I apply? What is the cost of attendance? How do I schedule a campus tour? When is New Student Orientation? How do I apply to live on-campus? How do I reset my password? How do I apply? What is the cost of attendance? How do I schedule a campus tour? When is New Student Orientation? How do I apply to live on-campus? How do I reset my password? Ask AI or Search Apply Now Contact Us WhatsApp Chat Facebook Messenger Live Chat Ask a Question Request More Information myBarry Apply Now Create Account Sign in Colleges and Schools Academic Support Enrollment Services Career & Experiential Learning Service-Learning Honors Program Library Undergraduate Graduate and Doctoral Adult learners School of Law (Orlando) Continuing Education Dual Enrollment Distance Education Athletics Campus Life Current Students Library Skill Development and Well Being Student Engagement Student Resources About Barry Academics Colleges and Schools Academic Support Enrollment Services Career & Experiential Learning Service-Learning Honors Program Library Admissions Undergraduate Graduate and Doctoral Adult learners School of Law (Orlando) Continuing Education Dual Enrollment Distance Education Student Life Athletics Campus Life Current Students Library Skill Development and Well Being Student Engagement Student Resources Alumni Give With our Catholic liberal arts heritage and over 100 degree programs, including nursing and marine biology, from bachelors through PhDs, we've got your options covered.\n\nFocus on arts and sciences, business, education, social work, communication, nursing, medical sciences, theology, or law. Take things further with personalized research and experiential learning opportunities, on and off-campus. Enhance your prospects with hands-on internships at some of the country's top organizations. Colleges and Schools College of Arts and Sciences School of Business and Public Administration College of Health Professions & Medical Sciences School of Mental Health and Social Work School of Nursing School of Podiatric Medicine School of Law (Orlando) Academic Support Center for Academic Success and Advising (CASA) Learning Center Registrar Testing Center Enrollment Services Enrollment Services Registrar Student Accounts Student Services Center The Career and Experiential Learning Team educates students and alumni on the essential job searching and life skills to propel them to succeed in the increasingly competitive global marketplace. Service-learning integrates relevant community service with course work and critical reflection to enrich the learning experience, foster social responsibility and civic engagement, and strengthen communities. The Honors Program at Barry is designed to challenge, enrich, and prepare especially motivated students to pursue their fullest potential. By participating in a rigorous curriculum rounded out by an array of edifying and interactive events, students explore crucial issues that we face in our daily lives. Students are given the space for discussion and debate and the opportunity to learn from experts in their fields. The Office of Financial Aid can assist with determining eligibility for the Honors Program. The Monsignor William Barry Memorial Library is located in the center of the beautiful Miami Shores campus of Barry University. The Library is named in loving memory of Monsignor William Barry, one of the founders of Barry University and an inspirational figure in the Catholic Church within the Archdiocese of Miami.\n\nThe extensive Library research collections include more than 950,000 physical items, over 40,000 print and on-line journal subscriptions, and several thousand on-line books and streaming video resources. At Barry University, you will experience a small community atmosphere where you can always rely on our administrators and faculty for advice, encouragement and personal attention. We take great pride in giving individual attention from the very beginning. You can start building a personal relationship with one of our admissions counselors who will help answer any questions, and guide you through the entire admissions and enrollment process. Undergraduate Admissions Find Your Program How to pay for college International Students Financial Aid FAQs Online Programs Plan Your Visit Graduate and Doctoral Admissions Find Your Program How to pay for college International Students Financial Aid FAQs Online Programs Adult learners Admissions FAQs Online Programs School of Law (Orlando) Admissions How to pay for college Admitted Students Continuing Education (CE) offers a variety of courses and non-credit programs designed to respond to the diverse educational interests and lifelong learning needs of individuals of all ages. We offer certificate, credential exam preparation, and licensure programs for professional and personal enrichment. High school students: Get a jump-start on your college education with dual enrollment courses from Barry University! You can earn high school and college credit at the same time, right at your own school. Barry University is committed to provide you with a dynamic and flexible approach to your degree pathway through our online courses and degree programs. We understand that balancing academics, work, and personal commitments can be challenging. That's why our online offerings are designed to fit seamlessly into your busy schedule, allowing you to pursue your educational goals without compromising on other important aspects of your life. We are committed to providing programs and services that are guided by Barry University's rich educational mission and intended to enhance your Barry experience. Through partnerships with others in the university community, we aim to create experiences that will help transform you into leaders for a just and humane world. We are an NCAA Division II school and a member of the Sunshine State Conference with 12 varsity teams, including men's baseball, basketball, golf, soccer and tennis; and women's basketball, golf, rowing, soccer, softball, tennis and volleyball. So far, we've won 24 NCAA championships, had 338 All-Americans, 413 Scholar All-Americans, and nine NCAA \"Women of the Year\" finalists, the most of any Division II school. Not bad at all, but we're going for more. Campus Life Dining Living on-campus Student Life Student Union For students currently enrolled in classes at Barry, we have a wealth of resources you can tap into to bring ease and efficiency to your university experience. Get the help you need with administrative or financial questions, or check out course catalogs to help plan your schedule by semester. All the information you need to excel is at your fingertips. Skill Development and Well Being Accessibility Services Campus Recreation Counseling & Psychological Services Health Promotion and Wellness Health Services Public Safety Student Engagement Engagement and Outreach Ministry and Community Outreach Student Life (Student and Family Engagement) Housing and Residence Life International Programs New Student Orientation Plan Your Visit Student Resources Campus Store Student Accounts Dual Enrollment Financial Aid IT Support Library Registrar Home Human Resources Save to My Pins Human Resources HR at Barry U We are a student-centered learning community that values diversity, collaboration, service, and professional growth. As a Catholic institution founded by the Dominican Sisters of Adrian Michigan, we believe that every person is a reflection of God and must be treated with dignity and respect. In joining the Barry community, you play an integral role in the lives of our students by furthering our institutional mission and core commitments . We are pleased to support our faculty, staff and students as we partner along in this transformational journey where learning leads to knowledge and truth, reflection leads to informed action, and a commitment to social justice leads to collaborative service. At Human Resources, we believe a healthy work environment is one where you can learn, grow, collaborate, and succeed. Our mission is to maximize each employee’s work experience by delivering quality service, ensuring equitable employment practices, offering professional development, providing comprehensive benefits and work/life balance initiatives, and fostering a work environment that attracts and inspires excellence. We strive to increase our knowledge and expertise, offer creative and innovative solutions, and be an employer of choice. Contact our Office Covid-19 Information It is our vision to continue to engage the Barry University community while being proactive and responsive to the changing needs of our faculty, staff and students through our communication and collaborative efforts. We accomplish our mission by upholding our values which are: Mutual respect and trust Integrity and honesty A diverse workforce Professional and ethical behavior Confidentiality Quality and excellence Professional development and career growth Mutual respect and trust Integrity and honesty A diverse workforce Professional and ethical behavior Confidentiality Quality and excellence Professional development and career growth Non-Discrimination Statement Barry University does not discriminate on the basis of race, creed, color, ethnicity, national origin, ancestry, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, familial status, marital status, pregnancy, age, disability status or veteran status. This policy applies to students, employees, applicants and trustees with respect to participation in any program, benefit, activity or student/employment opportunity offered by the University. Every member of the University community is expected to uphold this policy as a matter of mutual respect and fundamental fairness in human relations. Every student of this institution has a responsibility to conduct himself/herself in accordance with this policy as a condition of enrollment. Further, every University employee has an obligation to observe Barry University policies and implementation of federal and state law as a term of employment. No person shall be retaliated against for reporting violations or concerns about prohibited discrimination or bias through appropriate University channels. Nothing in this non-discrimination statement shall require Barry University to act in a manner contrary to the beliefs and teachings of the Catholic Church or the University mission statement. Benefits Barry University offers a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees that includes medical, dental, vision, life, retirement, tuition assistance, paid-time off, holiday pay, work/life balance initiatives such as wellness programs, spirituality in the workplace and training and development opportunities. Please click on the flip book below for more information. Benefits Guide 2026/27 Career Opportunities Thank you for considering Barry University as your future employer. Barry University is an equal opportunity employer. How to apply and what to expect: You will be prompted to create an account to submit your application. Please do not use all caps when entering your name. Complete all sections of the application in its entirety to include all relevant education, experience, and contact information. In addition to the application, the employment process will consist of a background check, reference check, interviews, and skill assessment testing when applicable. All applications are stored on a secure site. Only authorized personnel have access to the information submitted. How to view the status of your application: You may sign into your account and view the status of your application(s) by accessing the Candidate Home page located on the upper right hand corner of the webpage. Student Jobs Human Resources is excited to support our students in obtaining an on-campus part-time position. Barry University is an equal opportunity employer. Positions are available to undergraduate, graduate, international, and federal work-study students. Students can earn money while attending classes through part-time employment. Working on campus allows you to manage your work hours around your class schedule and gain valuable work experience related to your field of study or interests. You will be prompted to create an account to submit your application. Please do not use all caps when entering your name. Complete all sections of the application in its entirety to include all relevant education, experience, and contact information. You may sign into your account and view the status of your application(s) by accessing the Candidate Home page located on the upper right hand corner of the webpage. In addition to the application, the employment process will consist of a background check, reference check and interviews. Once selected for the position, you will be required to complete onboarding activities. Onboarding Details Welcome to Barry U Welcome to Barry University! We are delighted you have joined our University community! You will be entitled to a full and rewarding position. With this privilege comes accountability and responsibility to make decisions, and a willingness to work toward positive outcomes and to be evaluated based on performance. You will be valued for your unique contribution in attaining University goals and furthering the University mission. Getting Started All new hires will be required to complete onboarding activities prior to their start date. A new hire notification email will be sent to all new hires with instructions on how to login to the Barry network and Workday. For assistance with your new hire activities please contact us at humanresources@barry.edu. Onboarding Activities In Workday May Include: Review contact and personal information Provide emergency contact information Enter direct deposit information Complete the federal withholding elections (W-4) Complete the employment eligibility verification (Form I-9). Employees are required to present valid identification to HR within 3 business days of hire date (the hire date means the first day of work for pay). Failure to comply will result in immediate termination of employment in compliance with the Immigration Reform and Control Act. Policy review and acknowledgement Acknowledge privacy and security agreement Obtain parking decal. Select benefit elections Photo upload I-9 Acceptable Documents Parking Decal Payroll Information Paychecks are issued to exempt (salaried) employees on a semi-monthly basis (15 th and last day of each month). Paychecks are issued to non-exempt (hourly) employees on a bi-weekly basis (every other Friday). To view the payroll calendar on our intranet site. All employees will be paid electronically via their direct deposit or by a VISA payroll card . Payroll Calendar VISA Payroll Card University ID At the completion of your onboarding activities, you may obtain your university employment identification. For Miami Shores new hires, please visit the Student Union office, room 103, located in the R. Kirk Landon Student Union building on N Miami Avenue ( Campus Map ). Visit the Student Union website for information about your employment ID card, also known as the BUC Card. For Law School new hires, please visit the IT office, room 113, located in the Euliano Law Library building. Dwayne O. Andreas School of Law Campus Map Verification We are utilizing The Work Number® by Equifax to complete all requests for verification of employment and income for our employees. Please visit www.theworknumber.com or by calling The Work Number at 1-800-367-5690 to obtain the verification needed. You may also submit a written request with a signed release for employment verification to: Human Resources 305-899-3679 Fax Please allow a minimum of 72 hours for your request to be processed. You may contact us at 305-899-3675 for further information or to check the status of your request. To obtain proof of employment or income via The Work Number, you will need: Direct employee consent A permissible purpose for access the information, as defined by the Fair Credit Reporting Act Direct employee consent A permissible purpose for access the information, as defined by the Fair Credit Reporting Act Get social! Connect with us! iMessage WhatsApp Chat Facebook Messenger Live Chat Ask a Question 👋  Need help? Chat with Bucky! Apply Now Contact us Visit us Menu About Barry Admissions Alumni Give Living on Campus myBarry The University Campus Map Career Opportunities Newsroom President Strategic Plan Title IX Compliance University Administration Be Social 11300 NE 2nd Avenue Miami Shores, FL 33161-6695 305-899-3000 University Non-Discrimination Statement Barry University does not discriminate on the basis of race, creed, color, ethnicity, national origin, ancestry, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, genetic information, familial status, marital status, pregnancy, age, disability status or veteran status. This policy applies to students, employees, applicants and trustees with respect to participation in any program, benefit, activity or student/employment opportunity offered by the University. Every member of the University community is expected to uphold this policy as a matter of mutual respect and fundamental fairness in human relations. Every student of this institution has a responsibility to conduct himself/herself in accordance with this policy as a condition of enrollment. Further, every University employee has an obligation to observe Barry University policies and implementation of federal and state law as a term of employment. No person shall be retaliated against for reporting violations or concerns about prohibited discrimination or bias through appropriate University channels. Barry University’s EASE Grant Performance Measures on Access Rate, Affordability Rate, Graduation Rate, Retention Rate and Postgraduate Employment Rate are specifically listed on the ICUF Dashboard at this link: icuf.org/dashboard . Accessibility Statement Accreditation Notice Copyright FERPA Notice Privacy Policy ©2025 Barry University, All Rights Reserved Sign in to use the pins Sign in Create account"
